ts count includes them. Need not add product_weight_g IS NOT NULL filter? \"已知商品重量平均值\" means average known weights. AVG ignores null. Do we filter product_weight_g IS NOT NULL? That would exclude categories all unknown, but \"按类目全部商品数取前10\" suggests all products for count. Avg should ignore null, not filter whole category. So no filter on weight, only nonnull category. Output category and avg.\n\nNeed only SQL no code fence. Include LIMIT. The question says \"两位\" means two decimals. Round avg 2. Maybe alias as avg_weight. Need category original value. Use product_category_name. \"非NULL类目\" means filter p.product_category_name IS NOT NULL. Since dimension policy default excludes null anyway. We include.\n\nNeed consider order tie \"同数按类目原值升序\". Order by product_count desc, p.product_category_name asc. We can't order by alias? We can use COUNT(*) DESC. Do not output count.\n\nSQL:\nSELECT p.product_category_name AS product_category_name,\n       ROUND(AVG(p.product_weight_g)::numeric, 2) AS avg_product_weight\nFROM products p\nWHERE p.product_category_name IS NOT NULL\nGROUP BY p.product_category_name\nORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, p.product_category_name ASC\nLIMIT 10;\n\nNeed cast AVG? avg(integer) returns numeric in PG. ROUND(numeric, int) works. If product_weight_g integer, AVG(int) returns numeric. No need. But safe use AVG(p.product_weight_g)::numeric. If avg returns numeric already. Either.\n\nNeed maybe alias \"avg_weight\". Only categories and average. Final.\n\nDouble-check \"按非NULL类目统计已知商品重量平均值两位\" could require only products with known weight? If we do WHERE weight IS NOT NULL, then category count for top10 would count known only, violating \"全部商品数\". They emphasize by all product count top10. So don't filter weight. Good.\n\nNeed consider \"商品重量平均值\" maybe weight in grams. No unit conversion. Round two. Good.\n\nFinal only SQL."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3008,"completion_tokens":889,"total_tokens":3897,"prompt_tokens_d